id: pm-slack-global-update-operands
title: Global npm update guard mistakes option values and redirect targets for packages
description: "Follow-up to PR #206 thread PRRT_kwDOSYpJkM64Vsdx: npm update -g --loglevel warn and npm update -g >output currently return no findings. Round AN only changes continuation splitting. A separate line-based operand policy must handle option values and redirections while preserving approved fixtures."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[2]: follow-up,"gh:unbraind/pm-slack#206"
created_at: "2026-11-17T08:44:27.402Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-17T09:09:57.078Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-17T09:09:57.044Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-17T09:09:57.044Z"
author: codex-sol
repro_steps: "Run globalNpmInstalls on 'npm update -g --cache /tmp/x' or 'npm update -g > update.log': the option value or redirect target reads as an operand, so the operandless rule does not apply and the line passes."
resolution: "Fixed in 1172f90: any update-family line (update, up, upgrade, udpate) with a global marker, or in a global-configured run, is a violation regardless of operands. Rejected fixtures cover --cache, a redirect, a comment, a named package and NPM_CONFIG_GLOBAL=true."
expected_result: "Every global update-family line is rejected, whatever its operands."
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-17T09:03:14.949Z",codex-sol,"Round AP fixing commit 1172f9023dfe7410ebfd7d8ee02dd592189beae0: every global update/up/upgrade/udpate is rejected without operand classification. New rejected fixtures: npm update -g --cache /tmp/x; npm update -g > update.log; npm update -g # nightly; npm up -g some-package; NPM_CONFIG_GLOBAL=true npm update. Added alias matrix across global markers and effective global/location environment scopes. Required package gates passed; all prior fixtures and real workflows pass. Left for orchestrator verification."
